/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/H2Gly3-formation.dat -- the glycylglycylglycine master as the sum of its fully dissociated form (the inverse of the records written from the master; a case declares one master and the closure activates the record reachable from it):
      Gly3(-1) + 2 H+  <=>  H2Gly3

  logK25 and dH are the PRINTED values of the sources below (standard state ideal solution at 1 mol/kg, 298.15 K):
      pK1 = 3.224, dH1 = 0.84 kJ/mol
      pK2 = 8.090, dH2 = 41.7 kJ/mol
  Source: Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231; standard state: hypothetical ideal solution of unit molality, 298.15 K, 0.1 MPa (Section 8, p. 359).
  This record carries the sum of the first 2 steps (the sign flips with the direction written).
  The constant-dCp term of the printed dCp is NOT carried: the record grammar has no place for it (a
  van't Hoff integral with a constant dCp is exactly the `analytic` A1, A3, A4 terms; proposed, not done).
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species H2Gly3; masters ( { ion Gly3; nu 1; } { ion H; nu 2; } );
      logK25 11.314; dH -42540; source "Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231 -- Section 8 summary, p. 359, and Section 7.34, p. 289: pK1 3.224, dH1 0.84 kJ/mol, pK2 8.090, dH2 41.7 kJ/mol (pK, dH_ion at 298.15 K)";
